{
  "name": "Route LLM prompts with Claude as primary and OpenAI as fallback",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7334ab7b-0574-4d94-90de-f6f2eb19d53a",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -368,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## Route LLM prompts with Claude as primary and OpenAI as fallback\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives a call from another workflow or webhook.\n2. Normalizes the input and defines primary and fallback models.\n3. Sends the request to the primary model (Claude).\n4. Checks the response; if it's not usable, switches to the fallback model (OpenAI).\n5. Merges and returns the results to the caller.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Configure API keys for Anthropic and OpenAI.\n- [ ] Set primary_model and fallback_model in the 'Settings' node.\n- [ ] Ensure external workflows can trigger this workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the conditions in 'Fallback needed?' to refine when to switch to OpenAI."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "393c0a1f-bd59-436b-a253-21bc119d5e32",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        192,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## Receive and normalize input\n\nHandles the call from external sources and normalizes the input for processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7c1c51a6-51c3-4418-b285-71faf37fe4d2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        656,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Configure and process primary model\n\nSets the model configurations and sends a request to the primary model, Claude."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a91cf01f-a51b-48f2-a95f-fcd874b36f54",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1104,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Evaluate primary response\n\nChecks if the primary model's response is usable."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "45ba7709-6a8b-4477-8a86-01e02ff03ce9",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1552,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Process fallback response\n\nSends a request to OpenAI if the primary response is not usable and checks the fallback response."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "91e51919-2685-4442-8454-906df633c3f1",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2000,
        192
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 352,
        "content": "## Merge and return results\n\nMerges results from either primary or fallback into a unified response."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2c34ba8d-7073-4d10-b908-498bdd434845",
      "name": "Trigger on Workflow Call",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "notes": "Entry point. Expects prompt, system, mode, max_tokens from the caller.",
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "system",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "mode",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "max_tokens",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "e082f30f-b18f-4c32-b09f-098bd8c6d0aa",
      "name": "Normalize Input Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "notes": "Fills in defaults so callers only need to send prompt.",
      "position": [
        480,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Accepts a call from another workflow or a test webhook.\n// mode is passed through so callers can ask for a cheaper or stronger model.\nconst b = $json.body || $json;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  prompt: b.prompt || '',\n  system: b.system || '',\n  mode: b.mode || 'quality',\n  max_tokens: b.max_tokens || 500,\n} }];\n"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "a7728877-bf4b-454a-bfb3-9be6526720af",
      "name": "Post to Claude API",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "notes": "First attempt. Retries twice on a network error before falling through.",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "maxTries": 2,
      "position": [
        900,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({model: $json.primary_model, max_tokens: $json.max_tokens, system: $json.system, messages:[{role:'user',content:$json.prompt}]}) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            }
          ]
        },
        "nodeCredentialType": "anthropicApi"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 1000
    },
    {
      "id": "e2629dbb-8a36-4466-9d9c-9586c49d2b33",
      "name": "Check Claude Response Usability",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "notes": "Checks the actual text field, not just the HTTP status.",
      "position": [
        1152,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Did the primary provider return usable content? Anything else counts as a miss,\n// including a 200 response with an empty body.\nconst r = $json;\nconst ok = r && r.content && r.content[0] && r.content[0].text;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ok: !!ok,\n  text: ok ? r.content[0].text : '',\n  model: $('Configure Models Settings').first().json.primary_model,\n  fallback_used: false,\n} }];"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "6a9574fd-86b1-4f94-915c-ed459d847a82",
      "name": "Decide on Fallback Requirement",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "notes": "Branches to OpenAI only when Claude's answer was empty.",
      "position": [
        1376,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "false",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.ok }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "92d993a7-9f89-4acd-9b42-982917bf5122",
      "name": "Post to OpenAI API",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "notes": "Only runs on a miss from Claude.",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "maxTries": 2,
      "position": [
        1600,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({model: $('Configure Models Settings').first().json.fallback_model, max_tokens: $('Configure Models Settings').first().json.max_tokens, messages:[{role:'system',content:$('Configure Models Settings').first().json.system},{role:'user',content:$('Configure Models Settings').first().json.prompt}]}) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": []
        },
        "nodeCredentialType": "openAiApi"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 1000
    },
    {
      "id": "7f624b4e-d79c-497f-acbf-b876f6580f96",
      "name": "Check OpenAI Response Usability",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "notes": "Same content check, applied to the OpenAI response.",
      "position": [
        1808,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Same check for the fallback provider. The caller can read `model` and\n// `fallback_used` to see which one actually answered.\nconst r = $json;\nconst ok = r && r.choices && r.choices[0] && r.choices[0].message && r.choices[0].message.content;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ok: !!ok,\n  text: ok ? r.choices[0].message.content : '',\n  model: $('Configure Models Settings').first().json.fallback_model,\n  fallback_used: true,\n} }];"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "f74f3b91-2dca-4370-8b76-939d35fca3c1",
      "name": "Return Merged Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge",
      "notes": "Whichever branch ran, its output continues here.",
      "position": [
        2048,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "append"
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 3.2
    },
    {
      "id": "set-settings-0001",
      "name": "Configure Models Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "notes": "Both model names live here, change them without touching any expression.",
      "position": [
        700,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "name": "primary_model",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "claude-haiku-4-5"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "name": "fallback_model",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    }
  ],
